1065 2096 Q 717 2278 534 2592 Q 352 2906 352 3302 Q 352 3757 569 4096 Q 787 4435 1164 4620 Q 1542 4806 2003 4806 Q 2554 4806 2954 4528 Q 3354 4250 3571 3722 Q 3789 3194 3789 2445 Q 3789 1664 3555 1104 Q 3322 544 2896 243 Q 2470 -58 1869 -58 L 1869 -58 z\nM 1965 2362 Q 2150 2362 2348 2403 Q 2547 2445 2732 2521 Q 2918 2598 3046 2688 Q 3123 2739 3148 2793 Q 3174 2848 3174 2963 Q 3174 3187 3104 3430 Q 3034 3674 2890 3885 Q 2746 4096 2525 4227 Q 2304 4358 2003 4358 Q 1709 4358 1472 4224 Q 1235 4090 1097 3856 Q 960 3622 960 3328 Q 960 3059 1085 2838 Q 1210 2618 1434 2490 Q 1658 2362 1965 2362 L 1965 2362 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(111.40625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p623baaa5e0\"><rect x=\"45.371281\" y=\"14.649\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Subscribers around the last price rise (k)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Subscribers fell about 8% over three months, from 152k to 140k, then recovered most of the loss within five months.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> customers react, but the core audience stays. The real risk is the short-term dip, not a permanent loss.</p>"},{"q":"If 10% of subscribers cancel, does the rise pay off? How many could cancel before it stops paying?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Monthly margin today: 180k × ($6.99 − $1.50) = <b>$988k</b>.</p> <p>After: 162k × ($8.49 − $1.50) = <b>$1,132k</b>, +$144k a month (about $1.7M a year).</p> <p>Break-even loss: 1 − 5.49 ÷ 6.99 = <b>21.5%</b>. Paloma can lose about 1 in 5 subscribers and still be no worse off.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> with last time's dip of about 8%, there's a wide safety margin.</p>"},{"q":"How would you roll it out?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Explain why</b>: more films, restored classics, better subtitles</li> <li><b>Annual plan</b> at a modest discount (e.g. $89 a year, about 13% off 12 × $8.49, and still above today's $83.88) to lock in loyal subscribers</li> <li><b>Keep existing subscribers at the old price for three months</b> to soften the dip</li> <li><b>Watch new sign-ups</b>, not just cancellations: the higher price may slow growth</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Raise the price to $8.49. Even if 10% of subscribers cancel, monthly margin rises by about $144k, and the rise only stops paying if more than 21.5% leave; last time the dip was about 8% and mostly recovered. Pair it with an annual plan and a three-month grace period for existing subscribers. Risk: slower sign-ups from new viewers. Next step: track cancellations and sign-ups weekly for three months after launch.","great":["Reads the chart for both the dip and the recovery","Computes break-even churn, not just one scenario","Thinks about sign-ups as well as cancellations","Proposes a rollout that softens the reaction"],"id":35,"slug":"paloma-streaming"}